A||N||3||bocefas||Quirky wipers||||5||
Z||000000||bocefas||11-04-2001||08:51 PM||||Ok, here's a dandy...sometimes(but not every time) when I hit a bump in the road my windshield wipers cycle.  It also happens(sometimes)when I use my turn signal or flip from high beam to low beam...My extremely astute deductive reasoning leads me to believe that there is a bad connection in the turn signal/dimmer/wiper switch...so my question is:  Is replacing the whole turn signal lever going to fix my problem, or do you think it is something else?||||reg||5
Z||000001||avengador1||11-04-2001||09:05 PM||||I just replaced mine and from what I saw replacing it, I don't think that is the solution. The wipers are activated in the column.The shaft turns inside the column to do this. To remove the signal stalk just pull it straight out!!! This would be a quick way to see if the shaft key is broken, make sure it's in the off position first. I replaced mine because you couln't read the lettering on it any more. If you have cruise control and are going to replace the stalk, tie a thin wire to the end(plug side) to aid in installing the new one. If you don't do this you will have a hard time fishing the wire back thru. I got mine from Rodney Dickman. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Camer015.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dslice||11-05-2001||12:08 AM||||The actual switch is inside the stearing column. Seems like a monster to get at. I just live with the my wipers going on at odd times.<P>------------------<BR>Rick<P>86GT<BR>84COUP<BR>http://home.mn.rr.com/gmfierogt||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||11-05-2001||08:22 AM||||It's not that hard to replace it. It just takes a few hours. You will need a steering wheel puller and a lock plate remover. You can get them at pep-boys or autozone. When I replaced my column switch I cut the switch off and spliced the new switch on the old harness. I couldn't get the plastic plug through all the junk in the column.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">   <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.||||reg||14
